matter|Issue noun, important intransitive verb and physical substance noun are separate source boundaries. Vietnamese preserves letter timing, apology context and microscope observation; no technical mass/weight equivalence is asserted.
overcrowded|Excess over usable space rather than simply busy is the meaning. Bus arrival causes waiting-room crowding in both languages; with complement and adjective syntax are checked.
so-called|Label may signal doubt or be neutral; noisy carriage example deliberately illustrates ironic doubt. Vietnamese retains the named quietness and actual conversations without implying a factual universal rule.
weight|Everyday heaviness meaning is kept without claiming technical equivalence to mass. Parcel and label comparison align in Vietnamese; noun article use concerns the particular parcel's weight.
author|Written-work creator rather than rights owner is the boundary. Novel questions example preserves feminine possessive content naturally; no ownership, license or human authorship evidence is inferred.
